    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-upside profile of **Junior Caminero**, who represents our strongest play at an 82.11 efficiency score. Facing Jacob Lopez and his unfavorable 5.06 xERA, **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from a projected +10% park factor and an elite xwOBA of 0.376, making him the cornerstone of our offensive strategy. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** serves as an elite tier option at 76.86; he draws a favorable matchup against Blade Tidwell, with wind blowing out providing an extra statistical boost that cements his status as a must-start despite a neutral park adjustment. **Caleb Durbin** also projects well at 66.32, capitalizing on the scarcity of stolen bases; his elevated SP skill score suggests he is well-positioned to exploit Jameson Taillon\u2019s 4.50 xERA while hitting in the optimal #3 hole.\n\nTactically, we are leaning into dynamic platoon edges to maximize efficiency. **Lars Nootbaar** and **Christian Yelich** see their scores buoyed by +11% and +13% platoon adjustments, respectively, which keep them firmly in the \"Strong\" start category despite mediocre park factors. **Trea Turner** remains a vital cog at 60.55; his stolen base upside is non-negotiable in our 5x5 build, even with a slight park-related penalty. The most difficult benching decision involved **Nelson Velazquez** (53.98), who narrowly missed a starting slot. While **Nelson Velazquez** benefits from Andrew Painter\u2019s 4.55 xERA, his regression due to the R/R platoon disadvantage and a lower relative floor compared to the outfield options forced him into the UTIL reserve. Owners should monitor the 31% rain risk surrounding **Carson Benge**; while his 57.62 score is strong, the weather could impact his plate appearance volume, though he remains a superior start to the current bench depth.",
